From b2df4fb4a92278cb8af3cf0251d58177f96c1956 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:57:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/32] fix(desktop): fold the narrow left drawer after a row
 selection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User ruling: picking a session (or a Bots roster / group row) on a narrow
viewport should land the user straight in the chat, not leave the drawer
over it. The desktop docked rail is untouched: the closer routes through
revealNarrowPane, which no-ops above the sidebar-collapse breakpoint.

- layout: export closeNarrowSidebarDrawer() (narrow-gated by construction)
- narrow overlay: a 'close' reveal intent is now side-scoped — the drawer
  may front ANY pane of the sessions zone (SESSIONS | BOTS strip) and the
  dispatcher cannot know which tab is active
- sessions rows: both list paths (flat + virtualized) funnel through one
  resume wrapper that folds after handing off to the caller
- bot & group rows: same helper via the plugin SDK; a failed bot open
  already surfaces its own notification, so the fold is never silent

E2E 390x844: drawer folds on selection, route lands the picked session;
1280: rail width byte-identical before/after selection.
